<section vertical-align="center">
  <grid spacing="none">
    <grid-item>
      <p role="eyebrow">Teaching analogy—not a quotation or proof</p>
      <h2>Teaching analogy: freedom in a seminar</h2>
      <freeform-block w="840" h="240">
        <shape preset="line" x="250" y="112" w="16" h="20" stroke="accent" stroke-width="3"></shape>
        <shape preset="line" x="264" y="112" w="16" h="20" stroke="accent" stroke-width="3" flip-v="true"></shape>
        <shape preset="line" x="278" y="112" w="16" h="20" stroke="accent" stroke-width="3"></shape>
        <shape preset="line" x="545" y="122" w="45" h="2" stroke="accent" stroke-width="3"></shape>
        <box type="content" x="0" y="15" w="250" h="210" sizing="fixed" vertical-align="center" background-color="surface" style="padding: 16pt 18pt;">
          <labels><label variant="outline">Claim</label></labels>
          <h3>No speaking rules means maximal freedom.</h3>
        </box>
        <box type="content" x="295" y="15" w="250" h="210" sizing="fixed" vertical-align="center" background-color="surface" style="padding: 16pt 18pt;">
          <labels><label variant="solid">Result</label></labels>
          <h3>Permission is not participation.</h3>
          <p>Confident voices monopolize time. Equal permission does not produce equal participation.</p>
        </box>
        <box type="content" x="590" y="15" w="250" h="210" sizing="fixed" vertical-align="center" background-color="surface" style="padding: 16pt 18pt;">
          <labels><label variant="outline">Revision</label></labels>
          <h3>Turn-taking enables more voices.</h3>
          <p>Interruption is limited, while each person’s claim to speak survives in a changed practice.</p>
        </box>
      </freeform-block>
      <p font-size="sm">The tangled line marks the internal problem: unrestricted speaking defeats the freedom it promised.</p>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>